From 05aa6450096db58faa68146f19f44afc5634b667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:50:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Let smk_free take a NULL pointer

The error path of smk_open_generic frees a Huffman tree chunk that is
still NULL when the header is rejected, and smk_close frees members of
a half-built object. With assertions enabled, opening a file that is
not a Smacker video aborts the program instead of returning NULL.
free(NULL) does nothing; drop the assertion.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments
---
 smk_malloc.h | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smk_malloc.h b/smk_malloc.h
index cf944e7..bd5a30f 100644
--- a/smk_malloc.h
+++ b/smk_malloc.h
@@ -25,11 +25,9 @@
 
 /**
 	Safe free: attempts to prevent double-free by setting pointer to NULL.
-		Optionally warns on attempts to free a NULL pointer.
 */
 #define smk_free(p) \
 { \
-	assert (p); \
 	free(p); \
 	p = NULL; \
 }
